{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "072X", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-leray}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b84a497e2a290ed60b65f5fcad0943f281fe5c3aa463af58f240a9a81d81c78c", "source_text": "The Leray spectral sequence", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0da0f0aa81a51b98d891c3f9046c5dbb48582772cb4ed1c304fcd81d26d10221", "unit_id": "tag:072X:title"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "072X", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c312fd1f7d6ac0b67887bc851c0a0de44917dbd9a923f51cdedc821eec87b9b5", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe key to proving the existence of the Leray spectral sequence is\nthe following lemma.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6c5c460f81487a7195600d33623f3735a1de847348c71c06904ac79f870d9ea1", "unit_id": "tag:072X:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "072X", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : (\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}), \\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C}) \\to\n(\\Sh(\\mathcal{D}), \\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{D})$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\textit{Mod}(\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0004": "$f_*\\mathcal{I}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-direct-image-injective-sheaf}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6ea1f3a7d11b23702a721c33cbd67ff9bd523a705274b64cb473366735c0a867", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ead4419166e5b48464a9f5aab12bbe358a4fc914c2e1e4a72e3f671384744a88", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of ringed topoi.\nThen for any injective object <MATH_0002> in\n<MATH_0003>\nthe pushforward <MATH_0004> is totally acyclic.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d20b7a84bb53068cbaa200bb0adffec4c0854a1f7240514646b4eeb7ffaac81c", "unit_id": "tag:072Z:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "072X", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\v C", "GROUPCLOSE_0001": "}", "GROUPOPEN_0001": "{", "MATH_0001": "$K$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0005": "$f$", "MATH_0006": "$u : \\mathcal{D} \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0007": "$K = h_V$", "MATH_0008": "$V$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0010": "$H^q(V, f_*\\mathcal{I})$", "MATH_0011": "$q > 0$", "MATH_0012": "$V$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0014": "$f$", "MATH_0015": "$\\mathcal{V} = \\{V_j \\to V\\}$", "MATH_0016": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0017": "$u$", "MATH_0018": "$\\mathcal{U} = \\{u(V_j) \\to u(V)\\}$", "MATH_0019": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0020": "$$\n\\check{\\mathcal{C}}^\\bullet(\\mathcal{V}, f_*\\mathcal{I})\n=\n\\check{\\mathcal{C}}^\\bullet(\\mathcal{U}, \\mathcal{I})\n$$", "MATH_0021": "$f_*$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-modules-lemma-morphism-ringed-topoi-comes-from-morphism-ringed-sites}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-injective-module-trivial-cech}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-cech-vanish-collection}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4cd681d1a03844a327696df557a9386561814d0cf35ca0466c738999b8db0b17", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:793ab24f08abc98fd9c93cd52fc6f886891e8084cb15196504005887247ac404", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a sheaf of sets on <MATH_0002>.\nBy\nModules on Sites, Lemma\n<REF_0001>\nwe may replace <MATH_0003>, <MATH_0004> by ``larger'' sites such\nthat <MATH_0005> comes from a morphism of ringed sites induced by a continuous\nfunctor <MATH_0006> such that\n<MATH_0007> for some object <MATH_0008> of <MATH_0009>.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nThus we have to show that <MATH_0010> is zero\nfor <MATH_0011> and all objects <MATH_0012> of <MATH_0013> when <MATH_0014> is given\nby a morphism of ringed sites. Let <MATH_0015>\nbe any covering of <MATH_0016>. Since <MATH_0017> is continuous we see that\n<MATH_0018> is a covering of <MATH_0019>.\nThen we have an equality of <GROUPOPEN_0001><ACCENT_0001><GROUPCLOSE_0001>ech complexes\n<MATH_0020>\nby the definition of <MATH_0021>. By\nLemma <REF_0002>\nwe see that the cohomology of this complex is zero in positive degrees.\nWe win by\nLemma <REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:59c00dc7c62e27f07f9a886f1fa8a4deaabfb27a18d5ded6e2ca7f3fd7381592", "unit_id": "tag:072Z:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "072X", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f_*$", "MATH_0002": "$f_* : \\textit{Ab}(\\mathcal{C}) \\to \\textit{Ab}(\\mathcal{D})$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5c9d1518d0f95d4a31fa9296bb401a029b78ddac26ef7d8a8da003288b9e5db8", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a20095e8066566d546908079a4efb224c8a2bcdf3309f8aa7b2a33727ee164fc", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nFor flat morphisms the functor <MATH_0001> preserves injective modules.\nIn particular the functor\n<MATH_0002> always\n transforms injective\nabelian sheaves into injective abelian sheaves.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:14ed2361cf1f51cf613737f27c148f7dee349498e4a984a64bb8558bbbaf3437", "unit_id": "tag:072X:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "072X", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : (\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}), \\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C}) \\to\n(\\Sh(\\mathcal{D}), \\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{D})$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$f_*\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{I}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-pushforward-injective-flat}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9984809c5954a1bb0afd928854ca6ced94088d7e7554081f693ca06d7c805c8f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e2c4caa3b68202a745f77a5b8cf7c4afb870eeef12a317187d5471ba69bc0ef9", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of ringed topoi.\nIf <MATH_0002> is flat, then <MATH_0003> is an injective\n<MATH_0004>-module\nfor any injective <MATH_0005>-module <MATH_0006>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1f4333d87f6f6794566083e3e4144399016c82cc61bf37ccd3df88876d62112d", "unit_id": "tag:0730:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "072X", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f^*$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-modules-lemma-flat-pullback-exact}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{homology-lemma-adjoint-preserve-injectives}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a90771c0b33b2235aa2499c869ed3292c0fcae5305f0ae088e21632ec1f30af4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:12bdc000abf1b4ac8eea75b979e98ecdc4d3510c09e5ae031fb852a6eeba3a0a", "source_text": "In this case the functor <MATH_0001> is exact, see\nModules on Sites, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nHence the result follows from\nHomology, Lemma <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f954a25bdfcc802f17cc57df94d8741a7794eb8934cc3e443c028a91ca66bec3", "unit_id": "tag:0730:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "072X", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}), \\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0002": "$H^0(U, -)$", "MATH_0003": "$U$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F} \\mapsto \\mathcal{F}(K)$", "MATH_0006": "$K$", "MATH_0007": "$\\Gamma(\\mathcal{C}, -)$", "MATH_0008": "$f_*$", "MATH_0009": "$f : (\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}), \\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C}) \\to\n(\\Sh(\\mathcal{D}), \\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{D})$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-limp-acyclic}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a54034abb168525f78f575d6b5f735e393046c13cab73fec8a62ecfe5155942c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7efba598be2d730b5f10c0f2993e1ea58c2cf026e0b325f9716143c54fe70987", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a ringed topos.\nA totally acyclic sheaf is right acyclic for the following functors:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> the functor <MATH_0002> for any object <MATH_0003> of <MATH_0004>,\n<STRUCT_0003> the functor <MATH_0005> for any\npresheaf of sets <MATH_0006>,\n<STRUCT_0004> the functor <MATH_0007> of global sections,\n<STRUCT_0005> the functor <MATH_0008> for any morphism\n<MATH_0009> of ringed topoi.\n<STRUCT_0006>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cef178ab17ac2d59e91573480602541a39f7481e11a75f8e1bc2c708c0f0a845", "unit_id": "tag:0731:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "072X", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$K = e$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Sh(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$R^if_*$", "MATH_0005": "$i > 0$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-modules-lemma-morphism-ringed-topoi-comes-from-morphism-ringed-sites}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-higher-direct-images}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:30dc0e37a79dedb11433a33267afb0187da3ebdce8c8e3fd1dbd1dfc6d7ffe16", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:98b0a066aa91917e034282e3d0e93ab7db0597aec76e0df23cff01eceb808c19", "source_text": "Part (2) is the definition of a totally acyclic sheaf.\nPart (1) is a consequence of (2) as pointed out in the discussion following the\ndefinition of totally acyclic sheaves.\nPart (3) is a special case of (2) where <MATH_0001> is the final object\nof <MATH_0002>.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nTo prove (4) we may assume, by\nModules on Sites, Lemma\n<REF_0001>\nthat <MATH_0003> is given by a morphism of sites. In this case we see that\n<MATH_0004>, <MATH_0005> of a totally acyclic sheaf are zero by the description of\nhigher direct images in\nLemma <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e5e852e79eb5c93daebd3ab23abbe0d4d4676af55e0675bddd6e9b7cb365eb93", "unit_id": "tag:0731:proof"}
